{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfhjpeg8zcmMCduQhCcR9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sc1dnw2jer2Rch5ZzztopL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_5_repair_1\ncd $D && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python - << 'EOF'\nimport re\nsrc=open('candidate.py').read()\nold=src[src.index('    # Concave score'):src.index('    # Per-person')]\nnew='''    # Concave score on the parent's fixed scale (8, as in the parent model, so\n    # the gambler's belief a, b alone sets the size of the felt surprise):\n    # 8 * (s - kappa * s^2). kappa = 0 is the parent; kappa > 0 puts the most\n    # random-looking surprise at a \"just-right\" level CENTER + 1 / (2 kappa).\n    kappa = pm.HalfNormal(\"kappa\", sigma=2.0)\n    diff = 8.0 * ((s_a - s_b) - kappa * (s_a**2 - s_b**2))\n\n'''\nsrc=src.replace(old,new)\nsrc=src.replace('''(quadratic, peaked) scoring of the felt surprise. It is parameterised as a\nlinear plus a non-negative quadratic coefficient on the centred surprise\n(peak = c0 + k_lin / (2 k_quad)), which is linear in the parameters and so\nfar better identified than an explicit target level times a sensitivity.''','''(quadratic, peaked) scoring of the felt surprise: one curvature parameter on\nthe parent's fixed decision scale, so no free sensitivity trades off against\nthe size of the surprise.''')\nsrc=src.replace('a = pm.Normal(\"a\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)','a = pm.Normal(\"a\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)').replace('b = pm.HalfNormal(\"b\", sigma=1.0)','b = pm.HalfNormal(\"b\", sigma=1.5)').replace('lam = pm.Normal(\"lam\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)','lam = pm.Normal(\"lam\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)')\nopen('candidate.py','w').write(src)\nEOF\nsed -n 60,110p candidate.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_d